{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the equation \\(\\frac{x}{x - a} + \\frac{x - b}{x - a - b} = \\frac{x - a}{x - 2a} + \\frac{x + a - b}{x - b}\\), we will simplify and compare both sides step by step.\n\nFirst, let's denote the left-hand side (LHS) and the right-hand side (RHS) of the equation:\n\\[\n\\text{LHS} = \\frac{x}{x - a} + \\frac{x - b}{x - a - b}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\text{RHS} = \\frac{x - a}{x - 2a} + \\frac{x + a - b}{x - b}\n\\]\n\nWe will simplify each term individually and try to find a common \\(x\\) that satisfies the equation.\n\n### Step 1: Simplify the LHS\nConsider the first term \\(\\frac{x}{x - a}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{x}{x - a}\n\\]\n\nConsider the second term \\(\\frac{x - b}{x - a - b}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{x - b}{x - a - b}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Simplify the RHS\nConsider the first term \\(\\frac{x - a}{x - 2a}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{x - a}{x - 2a}\n\\]\n\nConsider the second term \\(\\frac{x + a - b}{x - b}\\):\n\\[\n\\frac{x + a - b}{x - b}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Combine and simplify\nWe need to find a common \\(x\\) that makes both sides equal. Let's test some values within the given constraints \\(2a > x > b > a > 0\\).\n\n","prefix_end":1038,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,23606,1124,11520,37018,45340,15170,87,481,264,92,488,1124,37018,45340,481,293,15170,87,481,264,481,293,92,284,1124,37018,45340,481,264,15170,87,481,220,17,64,92,488,1124,37018,45340,488,264,481,293,15170,87,481,293,11035,701,582,686,39721,323,9429,2176,11067,3019,553,3019,382,5338,11,1077,594,78064,279,2115,24413,3108,320,43,11961,8,323,279,1290,24413,3108,320,49,11961,8,315,279,23606,510,59,9640,59,1318,90,43,11961,92,284,1124,37018,45340,15170,87,481,264,92,488,1124,37018,45340,481,293,15170,87,481,264,481,293,532,59,921,59,9640,59,1318,90,49,11961,92,284,1124,37018,45340,481,264,15170,87,481,220,17,64,92,488,1124,37018,45340,488,264,481,293,1